            <ArticleTitle>Dextrocardia and two-vessel percutaneous intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>61-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dextrocardia is rare and percutaneous intervention in such patients presents additional challenges to the operator. This report describes successful two-vessel angioplasty and stenting, including a chronic, sub-totally occluded proximal left anterior descending artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
